  "title": "What plane glue does to creation is local",
  "subject": "How plane glue disturbs the touching rule and the twin rule",
  "conclusion": "On 191 spaces with exact creation maps, the touching rule holds wherever the removal's side leaves the cut free and fails only where glue constrains it; a glue line joining an atom's twin class is always a doubled-square line meeting two or more of its ports, and an atom splits only by the points of a line it emits into a planar brace. Planar lines see which port a removal entered by, while atom lines do not.",
